1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,562
Oh, it's a quarter to four,

2
00:00:03,562 --> 00:00:05,956
and I have a production meeting at four.

3
00:00:05,956 --> 00:00:08,934
I planned to take you for a ride in Central Park

4
00:00:08,934 --> 00:00:10,934
in a horse and carriage.

5
00:00:10,934 --> 00:00:11,912
Harry, I'd love to,

6
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:13,912
but I have work to do.

7
00:00:13,912 --> 00:00:17,077
OK. We'll walk back to your office with you.

8
00:00:17,077 --> 00:00:20,846
It's so nice out.

9
00:00:20,846 --> 00:00:22,873
I decided to forget about my accounting problems

10
00:00:22,873 --> 00:00:25,324
and just enjoy this beautiful spring day.

11
00:00:25,324 --> 00:00:28,893
Take the time, Susan.

12
00:00:28,893 --> 00:00:29,780
I know I should,

13
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:32,758
but ... well, there are too many things to do.

14
00:00:32,758 --> 00:00:35,008
I understand.

15
00:00:35,008 --> 00:00:38,116
I'll go for a ride with Michelle.

16
00:00:38,116 --> 00:00:38,714
Right.

17
00:00:38,714 --> 00:00:43,692
Well, I had a really nice time.

18
00:00:43,692 --> 00:00:44,669
So did I.

19
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:45,669
So did I.

20
00:00:45,669 --> 00:00:48,314
I'm sorry you can't come with us, Susan.

21
00:00:48,314 --> 00:00:51,045
So am I.

22
00:00:51,045 --> 00:00:54,603
Bye-bye.

23
00:00:54,603 --> 00:01:01,226
Harry! Michelle! Can you wait till I make a phone call?

24
00:01:01,226 --> 00:01:01,559
Sure.

25
00:01:01,559 --> 00:01:16,949
Susan Stewart's office.

26
00:01:16,949 --> 00:01:17,974
Sam, this is Susan.

27
00:01:17,974 --> 00:01:19,667
Hi. How was lunch?

28
00:01:19,667 --> 00:01:19,967
Fine.

29
00:01:19,967 --> 00:01:20,805
You're late.

30
00:01:20,805 --> 00:01:25,316
The production department's waiting in the conference room.

31
00:01:25,316 --> 00:01:26,361
I know.

32
00:01:26,361 --> 00:01:29,339
Ask Paul Smith to fill in for me.

33
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:30,954
He knows everything about the production schedule,

34
00:01:30,954 --> 00:01:32,317
and he can answer any questions.

35
00:01:32,317 --> 00:01:32,621
Right.

36
00:01:32,621 --> 00:01:33,837
Don't tell any one,

37
00:01:33,837 --> 00:01:37,141
but I'm taking a little time to smell the flowers.

38
00:01:37,141 --> 00:01:37,833
Good for you.

39
00:01:37,833 --> 00:01:39,004
It'll be our secret.

40
00:01:39,004 --> 00:01:41,626
But schedule another production meeting for tomorrow.

41
00:01:41,626 --> 00:01:42,751
I'll be back

42
00:01:42,751 --> 00:01:45,276
for my six o'clock appointment with Mr. Ozawa.

43
00:01:45,276 --> 00:01:45,800
OK, Susan.

44
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:47,207
And have a nice afternoon.

45
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:48,707
Thanks.

46
00:01:48,707 --> 00:02:29,898
She likes you.

47
00:02:29,898 --> 00:02:32,908
I know. I like her.

48
00:02:32,908 --> 00:02:34,263
How'd you do it?

49
00:02:34,263 --> 00:02:35,854
We had a talk.

50
00:02:35,854 --> 00:02:36,521
About what?

51
00:02:36,521 --> 00:02:37,832
Life.

52
00:02:37,832 --> 00:02:40,065
And what did you decide?

53
00:02:40,065 --> 00:02:43,065
That's a secret ... between us women.
